{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/813275-2ed-bloodline-qedeshah","id":813275,"title":"[2ED] Bloodline: Qedeshah","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-21T04:18:38-08:00","id":813275,"title":"[2ED] Bloodline: Qedeshah","content":"<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nQ4PFxa1UDQ0qO6cs8u1UEZjd7HBKBu2GLXhw8Bl6Jc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Another conversion of a Bloodline to 2E mechanics.</a><br /> <br /> Feedback is appreciated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T19:20:27-08:00","id":815821,"title":"","content":"I for one think that a good change would be to say that Males CAN be embraced, but not &quot;activate&quot; the bloodline.<br /> <br /> Because as &quot;Mothers&quot; they should have childer of both genders...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T19:34:38-08:00","id":815827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/813275-2ed-bloodline-qedeshah?p=815821#post815821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I for one think that a good change would be to say that Males CAN be embraced, but not &quot;activate&quot; the bloodline.<br /> <br /> Because as &quot;Mothers&quot; they should have childer of both genders...</div> </div> </div> </div>So, you're suggesting revise the Bloodline Bane from &quot;horrible death to male childer&quot; to simply an inability to manifest the Bloodline for men? Huh. That actually works, especially if those childer go on to other Bloodlines, where they may likely serve as the eyes and ears of the Hierodules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-14T15:28:23-07:00","id":1341329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/813275-2ed-bloodline-qedeshah?p=815827#post815827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, you're suggesting revise the Bloodline Bane from &quot;horrible death to male childer&quot; to simply an inability to manifest the Bloodline for men? Huh. That actually works, especially if those childer go on to other Bloodlines, where they may likely serve as the eyes and ears of the Hierodules.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Seems like a valid and interesting twist. And then one or two steps later one of those kindred who joined other bloodlines embraces a female childe - and she unknowingly turns Qedeshah on her own. double twist.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As an aside, wasn't there a Daeva bloodline also nicknamed Hierodules? The Naditu, i think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-14-2019, 06:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-14T18:53:33-07:00","id":1341375,"title":"","content":"I'd allow them to embrace Males but not let them join the bloodline.<br /> <br /> <br /> After all their place is to &quot;Mother&quot; Kindred<br /> <br /> And maybe a bloodline gift that lets them embrace someone into another clan....<br /> <br /> just noticed my old post saying same thing had forgotten it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-15T05:46:22-07:00","id":1341427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/813275-2ed-bloodline-qedeshah?p=1341375#post1341375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd allow them to embrace Males but not let them join the bloodline.<br /> <br /> <br /> After all their place is to &quot;Mother&quot; Kindred<br /> <br /> And maybe a bloodline gift that lets them embrace someone into another clan....<br /> <br /> just noticed my old post saying same thing had forgotten it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, we were even discussing and riffing on your idea. It's a solid one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-15T10:19:09-07:00","id":1341466,"title":"","content":"I like these. Several points, which may or may not deviate from the 1e version more significantly.<br /> <br /> 1. As others have well pointed out, these need to be able to &quot;mother&quot; Kindred of both genders. Suggest: the male so embraced suffers 24 hours and then emerges a Revenant with a particular condition that causes them to adhere to the clan of the first Kindred whose Vitae they drink. The purging process burns out their Mekhet linkage while retaining blood sympathy with their &quot;mother&quot;. Such &quot;prodigal sons&quot; then spread the cult-like nature of the bloodline and can cause spontaneous manifestation in females they embrace, later. All this assumes of course that the experience of their embrace doesn't drive them to draugr immediately....<br /> <br /> 1.b As the flavor text indicates &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">creating offspring now involves a considerably different process than before, both acts are still wet with blood and wracked with pain.&quot; </span></span>Yet creating female offspring is arguably easier and less bloody than mortal birth. Suggest extending the 24 hour pain period to embraces of females as well, along with the sires' sympathy and frenzy effect (which embracing within Tarahah would avoid). Thus females become Mekhet Qedeshah, while males that don't immediately fall to draugr (in the confines of your Tarahah haven, note) are sent out to become themselves.<br /> <br /> 2. There is likely a higher incidence of Undead Menses among the bloodline. This is worth a note.<br /> <br /> 3. The Qedeshah may take an inordinate interest in Dhampir, generally, and the ways in which a vampire might quicken their flesh to generate conception, specifically.<br /> <br /> 4. Their Devotions are all single-Discipline and look like sufficient deviations from baseline such that they should include a second--even a single-dot of another Discipline.<br /> <br /> 5. Being forced to roll Humanity to use the Kiss almost sounds like it should be a baseline vampire thing. As it is it seems odd for the Qedeshah, though I get the objective of encouraging them to retain high Humanity. --Is there latitude to weave Humanity requirements or contributions throughout the Devotions? Such that a low-Humanity bloodline member will just find their powers less useful? (In other words, they function less-well as a mother, but not as a seductive vampiress.)<br /> <br /> There is a lot of potential in these, especially as subversive elements pushing Kindred as a whole to spread, in opposition to the natural selfish interests of the vampiric conservative side.<br /> <br /> Especially like their moralistic approach to the embrace: blessing others with suck, so to speak.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12493,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","user":"Khanwulf","date":". 10-15-2019, 01:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-15T17:04:02-07:00","id":1341523,"title":"","content":"1-3 i liked very much and wholy agree with. Damn, i can half imagine some kind of bloodline bane/taint extrapolating devotions &amp; such from undead menses.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/813275-2ed-bloodline-qedeshah?p=1341466#post1341466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4. Their Devotions are all single-Discipline and look like sufficient deviations from baseline such that they should include a second--even a single-dot of another Discipline.</div> </div> </div> </div>This i'm somewhat unsure about, but then still have to get used to how bloodlines, their singular banes &amp; devotions work in 2e - or my own thoughts on unded menses - might fit in or not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/813275-2ed-bloodline-qedeshah?p=1341466#post1341466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">5. Being forced to roll Humanity to use the Kiss almost sounds like it should be a baseline vampire thing. As it is it seems odd for the Qedeshah, though I get the objective of encouraging them to retain high Humanity. --Is there latitude to weave Humanity requirements or contributions throughout the Devotions? Such that a low-Humanity bloodline member will just find their powers less useful? (In other words, they function less-well as a mother, but not as a seductive vampiress.)<br /> <br /> There is a lot of potential in these, especially as subversive elements pushing Kindred as a whole to spread, in opposition to the natural selfish interests of the vampiric conservative side.<br /> <br /> Especially like their moralistic approach to the embrace: blessing others with suck, so to speak.</div> </div> </div> </div>Motherly doesn't have to be either moralistic or humane, one might say.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-15T18:23:00-07:00","id":1341539,"title":"","content":"OMG I love these guys!!!<br /> <br /> Shekinah the Queen of Heaven was a real figure in early Judaic theology. Thank you for doing this conversion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T12:19:41-07:00","id":1341676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/813275-2ed-bloodline-qedeshah?p=1341523#post1341523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Motherly doesn't have to be either moralistic or humane, one might say.</div> </div> </div> </div>No it doesn't. I suspect that the 1e version these are drawn from takes that stance, but it is not necessary.<br /> <br /> At base, the Bloodline should revolve around the idea that they are in favor of unrestricted embrace (procreation), advise on the wisdom of a given embrace (matchmaking), and guide the young toward adulthood (counseling) so progeneration may continue. In the final facet they collide head-on with the Lancea, which proports to offer spiritual guidance and solace for the lost vamps; you could think of the conflict as between matriarchal and patriarchal family modes, if you wish.<br /> <br /> There is a mystic link back to the idea of procreation and its act as sacred, mixed up with some personified figures of such, but that can be looked at as scaffolding or foundation--as you like. <br /> <br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T13:10:13-07:00","id":1341692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/813275-2ed-bloodline-qedeshah?p=1341676#post1341676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No it doesn't. I suspect that the 1e version these are drawn from takes that stance, but it is not necessary.<br /> <br /> At base, the Bloodline should revolve around the idea that they are in favor of unrestricted embrace (procreation), advise on the wisdom of a given embrace (matchmaking), and guide the young toward adulthood (counseling) so progeneration may continue. In the final facet they collide head-on with the Lancea, which proports to offer spiritual guidance and solace for the lost vamps; you could think of the conflict as between matriarchal and patriarchal family modes, if you wish.<br /> <br /> There is a mystic link back to the idea of procreation and its act as sacred, mixed up with some personified figures of such, but that can be looked at as scaffolding or foundation--as you like.</div> </div> </div> </div>In a chronicle i started as player but eventually took ST duties for a time, a brood of Qedeshah came in contact with a cabal of Dammitic Creed kabalists and banded together in a congregation off their own, Beit Leilot, the House of Night, also known as house of lilith, Qlipothic reflection of the Shekinah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T19:23:12-07:00","id":1341763,"title":"","content":"already crudely emulate the &quot;Blood Sympathy&quot; part of Ordo Dracul?<br /> <br /> Maybe a Devotion that Copies the Ability of a Mass Embrace.<br /> <br /> or the Coil its Based on? <br /> <br /> or Just say that More then a few try to learn the Coil of the Voivode?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T05:32:50-07:00","id":1342059,"title":"","content":"If you\u2019re going to change the bane I recommend something that encourages them to form large family groups like must interact with a number of kindred each night equal to their Blood Potency or gain a level of the tempted condition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T09:09:05-07:00","id":1342093,"title":"","content":"Good suggestion <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4714\" data-vbnamecard=\"4714\">Live Bait</a>. To be clear, I don't think the humanity roll is a bad thing mechanically, it just seems a tad odd to have something that represents how well the vampire can disguise their monstrous hunger as a bane for the motherly bloodline. <br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/813275-2ed-bloodline-qedeshah?p=1341692#post1341692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In a chronicle i started as player but eventually took ST duties for a time, a brood of Qedeshah came in contact with a cabal of Dammitic Creed kabalists and banded together in a congregation off their own, Beit Leilot, the House of Night, also known as house of lilith, Qlipothic reflection of the Shekinah.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Qedeshah make very interesting candidates for a &quot;Lilith&quot; bloodline. Their origins point to such a connection, but they are not the only bloodline to make that kind of assertion. The Asam, for example, look like excellent candidates for a connection back to some goddess-monster figure.<br /> <br /> So I thought a bit... what if there were a bloodline under each clan that claimed connection back to the Lilith-ish figure of mythology? What if... they were all correct? And in some way the vampiric progeny of Lilith start/started clanless (revenants?) and when adopted acquired the bloodline appropriate to their ancestry?<br /> <br /> Something like that... have cake... eat too, something.<br /> <br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T09:22:07-07:00","id":1342098,"title":"","content":"Bane and boon should reenforce the behaviour expected of the bloodline and ideally play off each other, it\u2019s why my Sangiovanni conversation ignore the humanity penalty to interacting with the living for a scene (Worded to prevent dragons from abusing it) when they use the blush of life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T09:44:20-07:00","id":1342106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/813275-2ed-bloodline-qedeshah?p=1342093#post1342093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good suggestion <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4714\" data-vbnamecard=\"4714\">Live Bait</a>. To be clear, I don't think the humanity roll is a bad thing mechanically, it just seems a tad odd to have something that represents how well the vampire can disguise their monstrous hunger as a bane for the motherly bloodline.<br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> The Qedeshah make very interesting candidates for a &quot;Lilith&quot; bloodline. Their origins point to such a connection, but they are not the only bloodline to make that kind of assertion. The Asam, for example, look like excellent candidates for a connection back to some goddess-monster figure.<br /> <br /> So I thought a bit... what if there were a bloodline under each clan that claimed connection back to the Lilith-ish figure of mythology? What if... they were all correct? And in some way the vampiric progeny of Lilith start/started clanless (revenants?) and when adopted acquired the bloodline appropriate to their ancestry?<br /> <br /> Something like that... have cake... eat too, something.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's certainly possible indeed. But then i guess my old chronicle in Rio de Janeiro had factions &amp; sub-factions aplenty without bringing more bloodlines with &quot;lilithian&quot; claims of origin into the mix.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T13:48:42-07:00","id":1342177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/813275-2ed-bloodline-qedeshah?p=1342106#post1342106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's certainly possible indeed. But then i guess my old chronicle in Rio de Janeiro had factions &amp; sub-factions aplenty without bringing more bloodlines with &quot;lilithian&quot; claims of origin into the mix.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The point was that if you wanted to tie bloodlines back to such a figure, it might be possible to do so at a rate of one per clan (i.e. five total). Thus getting some kind of broader influence going instead of restricting it to one clan or so.<br /> <br /> Honestly this all sounded better in my head. If you want bloodlines to claim they come from a mythic figure why not? If there are competing claims why not?<br /> <br /> After all if Lilith or some other ur-vampire is wandering your nights her first comment is probably going to be &quot;why do I care?&quot;<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T16:51:46-07:00","id":1342223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/813275-2ed-bloodline-qedeshah?p=1342177#post1342177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The point was that if you wanted to tie bloodlines back to such a figure, it might be possible to do so at a rate of one per clan (i.e. five total). Thus getting some kind of broader influence going instead of restricting it to one clan or so.<br /> <br /> Honestly this all sounded better in my head. If you want bloodlines to claim they come from a mythic figure why not? If there are competing claims why not?<br /> <br /> After all if Lilith or some other ur-vampire is wandering your nights her first comment is probably going to be &quot;why do I care?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, i very much got the idea. It's just that a cult of Lilith taking on an unlife of its own can be messy enough on its own in a city where Crone and Sanctum both took something of a beating in the aftermath of dealing with another syncretic cult/bloodline combo going rogue/apocalyptic on the other kindred and masquerade in general. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-22T12:53:50-07:00","id":1342998,"title":"","content":"curious ideas how a <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Qedeshah </span></b></span></span></div>who spontaneously exhibited the bloodline would adapt if that's being entertained as a notion it needs to be explored a bit I think.<br /> <br /> Think Daddy would Try setting up a meeting with Grandma?<br /> <br /> or other ideas?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-24T09:21:20-07:00","id":1343439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/813275-2ed-bloodline-qedeshah?p=1342998#post1342998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">curious ideas how a <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Qedeshah </span></b></span></span></div> <br /> <br /> who spontaneously exhibited the bloodline would adapt if that's being entertained as a notion it needs to be explored a bit I think.<br /> <br /> Think Daddy would Try setting up a meeting with Grandma?<br /> <br /> or other ideas?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Bloodline skipping a generation ain't exactly uncommon - it's when the generation gap extends to two or more, possibly making one's sire just as ignorant as the PC or NPC, that things start to get messily interesting. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (Bonus if some ancestor came through &quot;the taint&quot; by diablerizing without knowing the just out of torpor remnant of some supposedly extinct ancient bloodline)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-24-2019, 12:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-24T09:51:08-07:00","id":1343448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/813275-2ed-bloodline-qedeshah?p=1343439#post1343439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Bloodline skipping a generation ain't exactly uncommon - it's when the generation gap extends to two or more, possibly making one's sire just as ignorant as the PC or NPC, that things start to get messily interesting. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (Bonus if some ancestor came through &quot;the taint&quot; by diablerizing without knowing the just out of torpor remnant of some supposedly extinct ancient bloodline)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Best way to do it is through blood sympathy. In the sense that you suddenly acquire enough with an unknown individual to start drawing you together. Which, for vampires, is a pretty horrifying situation... you're drawn to an unknown, presumed elder force of a race of cannibalistic monsters--good luck!<br /> <br /> And it would be &quot;mommy&quot;, since daddy is only a carrier of the bloodline. It would manifest like a gender-specific recessive genetic trait. Only it's the genetics of the Blood, not the human it rides....<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-24T10:21:09-07:00","id":1343455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/813275-2ed-bloodline-qedeshah?p=1343448#post1343448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Best way to do it is through blood sympathy. In the sense that you suddenly acquire enough with an unknown individual to start drawing you together. Which, for vampires, is a pretty horrifying situation... you're drawn to an unknown, presumed elder force of a race of cannibalistic monsters--good luck!<br /> <br /> And it would be &quot;mommy&quot;, since daddy is only a carrier of the bloodline. It would manifest like a gender-specific recessive genetic trait. Only it's the genetics of the Blood, not the human it rides....</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yes, the delicious occult vagaries of blood sympaathy and other peculiarities of kindred vitae or related ichors.<br /> <br /> Could be worse - imagine your &quot;sire&quot; was a strix - and it had divided before &quot;embracing&quot;. And now you have a bird of shadow &amp; smoke as brother or uncle/aunt. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-24T14:04:16-07:00","id":1343494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/813275-2ed-bloodline-qedeshah?p=1343455#post1343455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh yes, the delicious occult vagaries of blood sympaathy and other peculiarities of kindred vitae or related ichors.<br /> <br /> Could be worse - imagine your &quot;sire&quot; was a strix - and it had divided before &quot;embracing&quot;. And now you have a bird of shadow &amp; smoke as brother or uncle/aunt. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Family reunions are always fun. Try the pecan pie. It's to die for.<br /> <br /> But seriously(ish?)--blood sympathy enables all manner of curious gyrations.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-24T15:17:22-07:00","id":1343502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/813275-2ed-bloodline-qedeshah?p=1343494#post1343494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Family reunions are always fun. Try the pecan pie. It's to die for.<br /> <br /> But seriously(ish?)--blood sympathy enables all manner of curious gyrations.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> For an extra complication, i remember reading something somewhere - possibly the Rome books, but wish i could point out where for sure - about one's mortal descendants also counting for blood sympathy....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-25T12:53:52-07:00","id":1343635,"title":"","content":"One could identify mortal relatives by the taste of their blood in the 1st edition VtR book. But nothing specific about how far backward sideways or forward it runs","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-26T11:10:43-07:00","id":1343814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/813275-2ed-bloodline-qedeshah?p=1343635#post1343635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One could identify mortal relatives by the taste of their blood in the 1st edition VtR book. But nothing specific about how far backward sideways or forward it runs</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, that was what i misremembered. It sort of stick in the mind because a ST used the accidental killing of a mortal descendant - one he was not aware of having - not only as an excuse to shake my character out of a frenzy, but a hook to leading him into learning more of this extended family he did not know.<br /> <br /> Anyway, thanks for correcting me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-26-2019, 02:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-26T21:48:26-07:00","id":1343920,"title":"","content":"Mortal family ties was an ongoing/recurring element in one setting I played. The family matriarch liked to keep an eye on her and her twin brother's mortal descendants. And more than once they ended up embracing a great grandchild, niece, nephew, cousin, etc. Or getting a kindred ally from another clan to do so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-27T06:05:23-07:00","id":1343975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/813275-2ed-bloodline-qedeshah?p=1343920#post1343920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mortal family ties was an ongoing/recurring element in one setting I played. The family matriarch liked to keep an eye on her and her twin brother's mortal descendants. And more than once they ended up embracing a great grandchild, niece, nephew, cousin, etc. Or getting a kindred ally from another clan to do so.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, that little bit from 1st edition VtR makes it all too simple for one to get into the whole ancestor-spirit, sometimes protecting, sometimes predating, when not both, angle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}